--------------------------------------------------------
1. NODE.JS
--------------------------------------------------------

>> Event Loop
- Node.js single-threaded hai but non-blocking I/O handle karta hai event loop ke through.
- Phases hote hain: Timers -> Pending Callbacks -> Idle/Prepare -> Poll -> Check -> Close Callbacks.
- Poll phase me I/O events process hote hain, Check phase me setImmediate() callbacks chalte hain.
- Microtasks (Promises, process.nextTick) HAR phase ke baad turant execute hote hain, macrotasks (setTimeout, setImmediate) se pehle.
- Interview tip: "process.nextTick > Promise microtask > setTimeout/setImmediate" priority order bolna.

>> libuv
- libuv ek C library hai jo Node.js ko async I/O deti hai (file system, networking, DNS).
- Ye thread pool (default size 4) maintain karta hai heavy/blocking operations ke liye (jaise fs, crypto, dns.lookup).
- Event loop khud libuv implement karta hai.
- Thread pool size UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE env variable se badha sakte hain.

>> Async/await & Promises
- Promise 3 states me hoti hai: pending, fulfilled, rejected.
- async/await Promise ke upar syntactic sugar hai - code synchronous jaisa dikhta hai but non-blocking rehta hai.
- try/catch async/await ke saath error handling ke liye use hota hai.
- Promise.all() - saari promises parallel me chalao, ek bhi fail hui to poora reject.
- Promise.allSettled() - sab complete hone tak wait, fail/success dono ka result milta hai.
- Promise.race() - jo pehle resolve/reject ho jaye.

>> Callbacks
- Traditional async pattern - function complete hone par ek callback function call hota hai.
- "Callback Hell" problem - nested callbacks se code unreadable ho jata hai (pyramid of doom).
- Error-first callback pattern Node.js convention hai: callback(err, result).
- Promises/async-await callback hell solve karte hain.

>> EventEmitter
- Node.js ka core module (events) jo pub-sub pattern implement karta hai.
- .on()/.addListener() - event listen karna, .emit() - event trigger karna, .once() - sirf ek baar sunna.
- Streams, HTTP server jaise bohot saare Node core modules EventEmitter se inherit karte hain.
- Memory leak ho sakta hai agar listeners properly remove na kiye jayein (removeListener/off use karo).

>> Streams & Buffers
- Buffer - raw binary data handle karne ke liye (fixed-size memory allocation, outside V8 heap).
- Streams - large data ko chunks me process karna, poora memory me load kiye bina.
- 4 types: Readable, Writable, Duplex (dono), Transform (modify karte hue pass karna).
- .pipe() method streams ko chain karne ke liye use hota hai.
- Real use-case: large file upload/download, video streaming, S3 se large object read karna.

>> Error Handling
- Sync errors: try/catch.
- Async errors: try/catch with async/await, ya .catch() Promises me.
- Uncaught exceptions: process.on('uncaughtException'), unhandled rejections: process.on('unhandledRejection').
- Custom Error classes bana ke operational vs programmer errors differentiate karna best practice hai.
- Lambda context me error handling important hai kyunki unhandled error se Lambda crash/retry trigger hota hai.

>> Performance & Memory
- Memory leaks common causes: global variables, closures holding references, un-cleared timers/listeners, caching without limits.
- V8 heap - Old space & New space (garbage collection generations).
- Tools: --inspect flag, Chrome DevTools, heap snapshots, clinic.js.
- Event loop blocking avoid karo - heavy CPU tasks ko worker threads me offload karo.

>> Cluster vs Worker Threads
- Cluster module: multiple Node.js processes (each with own event loop & memory) fork karta hai, load balance karta hai multiple CPU cores par. Achha hai for scaling HTTP servers.
- Worker Threads: same process ke andar multiple threads, memory share kar sakte hain (SharedArrayBuffer). Achha hai CPU-intensive tasks ke liye (image processing, calculations) bina event loop block kiye.
- Lambda context: Lambda already isolated execution environment deta hai per invocation, so cluster module wahan directly relevant nahi hota, but worker threads CPU-heavy tasks ke liye use ho sakte hain.

