5. API GATEWAY
--------------------------------------------------------

>> REST API
- Full-featured API Gateway type - request/response transformation, API keys, usage plans, caching support karta hai.
- Zyada configuration options but thoda zyada cost & latency HTTP API se compare karke.

>> HTTP API
- Newer, lightweight, cheaper aur faster API Gateway type.
- Limited features REST API ke comparison me (less transformation options) but most common use-cases ke liye sufficient hai.
- Native OIDC/OAuth2 support built-in.

>> API -> Lambda
- Lambda Proxy Integration: full request API Gateway se Lambda ko event object me forward hota hai, Lambda specific JSON format me response return karta hai.
- Lambda Non-Proxy: mapping templates (VTL) use karke request/response transform karte hain.

>> Authentication
- "Who are you" verify karna.
- Options: Cognito User Pools authorizer, Lambda custom authorizer (token-based or request-based), IAM authentication.

>> Authorization
- "What are you allowed to do" - authenticated user ko specific resource/action ki permission hai ya nahi.
- Lambda authorizer custom logic likh sakta hai (roles, scopes check karke).
- IAM policies bhi resource-level authorization define kar sakti hain.

>> Cognito (with API Gateway)
- Cognito User Pool authorizer directly API Gateway me attach ho sakta hai.
- Client JWT token (from Cognito) Authorization header me bhejta hai, API Gateway automatically validate karta hai before Lambda tak request pahunchne se.

>> CORS
- Cross-Origin Resource Sharing - browser security jo different-origin API calls ko block karta hai by default.
- API Gateway me CORS enable karna padta hai (Access-Control-Allow-Origin headers, preflight OPTIONS request handle karna).
- Common interview gotcha: proxy integration me CORS headers Lambda response se bhi return karne padte hain.

>> Throttling
- Rate limiting - kitne requests per second allow hain (steady-state rate + burst limit token bucket algorithm).
- Account level, stage level, aur per-method/usage-plan level throttling configure ho sakti hai.
- 429 "Too Many Requests" error throttle hone par aata hai.

>> Validation
- Request validation API Gateway level pe hi ho sakti hai (JSON schema based) - Lambda tak invalid request pahunche hi na.
- Query params, headers, body sabko validate kar sakte hain - isse unnecessary Lambda invocations bachti hain (cost + performance benefit).

>> Error Handling
- Gateway responses customize kar sakte hain (4XX, 5XX errors ke liye custom messages/format).
- Lambda se throw hone wale errors ko proper HTTP status codes me map karna important hai (mapping templates ya proxy integration me statusCode explicitly return karke).

