8. AWS COGNITO
--------------------------------------------------------

>> User Pool
- User directory hai - sign-up, sign-in, user management (password reset, MFA, email verification) handle karta hai.
- Successful login ke baad JWT tokens issue karta hai.

>> Identity Pool
- Temporary AWS credentials deta hai (via STS) authenticated/unauthenticated users ko taaki wo directly AWS resources access kar sakein (e.g., S3 se directly upload).
- User Pool se authenticate hone ke baad Identity Pool credentials exchange karne ke liye use hota hai.

>> Authentication vs Authorization
- Authentication = identity verify karna (tum kaun ho - login/signup).
- Authorization = permission verify karna (tumhe kya access hai - roles/scopes).

>> JWT (JSON Web Token)
- Self-contained token jisme header, payload (claims), signature hota hai - base64 encoded.
- Server bina database lookup ke verify kar sakta hai (signature check karke) ki token valid hai.

>> Access/ID/Refresh Tokens
- ID Token: user ki identity info (claims like email, name) - "who is this user".
- Access Token: API/resource access ke liye use hota hai, scopes/permissions carry karta hai.
- Refresh Token: naye access/ID tokens generate karne ke liye jab existing expire ho jayein, bina dobara login kiye - long expiry hota hai.

>> Cognito + API Gateway
- Cognito User Pool ko API Gateway authorizer ke roop me directly attach kar sakte hain.
- Client request me Authorization header me access token bhejta hai, API Gateway automatically validate karke Lambda ko forward karta hai (agar valid ho).

