9. TESTING
--------------------------------------------------------

>> Jest
- Popular JavaScript/TypeScript testing framework - test runner, assertion library, mocking sab built-in.
- ts-jest ya babel-jest use hota hai TypeScript support ke liye.

>> Unit Testing
- Individual function/module ko isolation me test karna, dependencies mock karke.
- Fast execute hota hai, business logic verify karta hai.

>> Integration Testing
- Multiple components/modules ko saath me test karna (e.g., Lambda handler + DynamoDB interaction, using real or local test DB).
- Real dependencies ya close-to-real (LocalStack, DynamoDB Local) use hote hain.

>> E2E Testing
- Poora system end-to-end flow test karna, jaise real user karta - API call se leke DB tak.
- Slowest but sabse zyada confidence deta hai ki real-world scenario me sab kaam kar raha hai.

>> Mocking
- Real dependency (API call, DB, external service) ki jagah fake/controlled implementation use karna taaki tests fast, isolated aur predictable rahein.

>> jest.fn()
- Ek mock function create karta hai jise track kar sakte hain (kitni baar call hua, kya arguments diye gaye) aur jiska return value control kar sakte hain.

>> jest.spyOn()
- Existing object ke method ko "spy" karta hai - real implementation call hoti hai by default but tracking milti hai, ya mockImplementation() se override bhi kar sakte hain.

>> mock()
- jest.mock('module-path') - poore module ko automatically mock kar deta hai (e.g., AWS SDK ko mock karna taaki real API call na ho tests me).

>> Test Coverage
- Metric jo batata hai kitna code tests se cover hua hai (statements, branches, functions, lines %).
- jest --coverage command se report milti hai. 100% coverage guarantee nahi karta ki bugs nahi hain, but useful indicator hai.

>> Cypress Basics
- E2E/UI testing framework, real browser me app ko test karta hai (user interactions simulate karke - click, type, navigate).
- Serverless APIs testing ke liye bhi use ho sakta hai (API testing mode me).

